text.section:
After the revocation of dissolution is authorized, the corporation may revoke the dissolution by filing with the Commission articles of revocation of dissolution that set forth:

The name of the corporation;


The effective date of the dissolution that was revoked;


The date that the revocation of dissolution was authorized;


If the corporation's board of directors revoked a dissolution authorized by the members, a statement that revocation was permitted by action by the board of directors alone pursuant to that authorization; and


If member action was required to revoke the dissolution, the information required by subdivision 3 of subsection A of § 13.1-904.
